From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Sun, 19 Apr 2026 15:23:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] board: freescale: gateway-dk: add hw self-test harness

Adds the small infrastructure that the per-chip self-tests in the
follow-up patch depend on:

  - hw_test.{h,c}: a test runner that prints aligned bracket-prefixed
    PASS/FAIL lines, a banner, and a final summary. Tests fill in a
    context struct and return an int; the harness owns the styling
    and the aggregate counting.
  - i2c_helpers.{h,c}: setup_i2c_muxed_device() wraps the
    'select PCA9545 channel, then get the device behind the mux'
    pattern that every per-component test reuses.
  - setup/Makefile: builds these two units; per-chip files are added
    in the next patch.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [product-specific]

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
